  "notes": "USAGE: {動揺|どうよう} primarily describes emotional disturbance or being mentally shaken. It's commonly used to describe reactions to shocking news or unexpected situations.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{動揺|どうよう}する (to be shaken/disturbed)\n・{動揺|どうよう}させる (to shake/disturb someone)\n・{動揺|どうよう}を{隠|かく}す (to hide one's agitation)\n・{動揺|どうよう}を{見|み}せる (to show one's agitation)\n\nHOMOPHONE:\n・{童謡|どうよう} (children's song) - same reading, different meaning\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n・{狼狽|ろうばい} (panic, confusion)\n・{混乱|こんらん} (confusion)\n・うろたえる (to be flustered)\n・{慌|あわ}てる (to panic, be in a hurry)",
